<title>THAILAND: TPI buys country's biggest crude tanker.</title>
<headline>TPI buys country's biggest crude tanker.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai Petrochemical Industry Plc has bought Thailand's first very large crude carrier (VLCC), a company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 268,540-tonne vessel Orapin Global arrived in Thailand on Tuesday with two million barrels of crude from Saudi Arabia to feed TPI's 65,000 barrel-per-day condensate splitter, he said.</p>
<p>TPI's unit --Thai International Tanker-- purchased the ship from Greece for $15 million. The official said the firm plans to buy three more crude tankers by next year.</p>
<p>The 20-year-old VLCC will be used primarily to transport crude oil, mostly from the Middle East, to TPI's plant.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
